# Dxun, the jungle landing (TSL, 003EBO, 421DXN, 401DXN): the galaxy map
# to Onderon, Atton's blockade talk and Colonel Tobin's hail (attond), the
# Exile at the Ebon Hawk's turret ("I'll man the turret": 421DXN's
# minigame, six fighters shot down, 600 XP) and Atton's word that they
# must land, the reception aboard on Dxun (ond_rece: Onderon asked after,
# Kreia's outpost; Atton stays with the Hawk), ashore with Mira and
# Bao-Dur: the crashed droid carrier (its salvageable parts, the skeletal
# corpse, the rusted computer port [Repair]ed and its core [Computer]
# repaired, the remote droids back on line), the three remote droids
# reactivated as DSimpson does (the first's weaponry, targeting and
# shields, the second's weaponry),
# the skeletal corpse in the open ground, the Zhug bounty hunters' camp
# on the far path: Dezanti asked who he is, Mira backed against him (+INF,
# DSimpson's "a real bounty hunter"), no surrender and the Duros fought,
# their camp's containers searched, the wreckage and the skeletal corpse
# behind it, and on into the jungle (402DXN).
# Starts from Nar Shaddaa's last checkpoint:
#   kjk playthrough tsl @nar_shaddaa_done data/routes/tsl/dxun_landing.route --god
# Walkthrough: DSimpson's "Onderon / Dxun" and "Dxun Jungle, Ebon Hawk
# Area" (context/walkthroughs/tsl/).
# Left: the reactor overloads (they blow the droids up), the rest of the
# droids' systems and patrol mode (the parts left are Zuka's wires'), the
# Zhugs' ground bag (GroundBagMetalCase: a placeable not useable).
#
# ASSUMES:
# - The party carries repair parts and computer spikes from the planets
#   before (15 parts, 2 spikes on the Sentinel's chain); the Exile's
#   Repair 5 and Computer 10 make the port 2 parts, its core 1 spike and
#   each droid's system 2 or 3 parts.
equip saber          # the Exile's own lightsaber in hand (003EBO_PC_Lightsaber; its
                     # template is a_give_quest_ls's pick for the Exile's level)
use Galaxymap
travel 7             # Onderon (planetary.2da): the blockade, 003EBO again
say I'll man the turret. # a_to_421dxn
talk                 # Atton (attond): Tobin's hail, the hits
module 421dxn
turrets              # the fighters, until the minigame's end leaves
talk                 # Atton after the turret (attond start 1): the movies
say We need to get to Onderon. # the reception (ond_rece, a_dxun_cs)
say Let's head to the outpost, then.
talk
party 7,1            # Mira (the Zhugs) and Bao-Dur (Kumus)
to tr_leave          # the ramp: the party screen, accepted
module 401dxn
use exp_comp@1       # the droid carrier's salvageable parts
use exp_comp@2
use g_tressklcorp004 # the skeletal corpse by the carrier
say [Repair] Fix the computer port.
say [Computer] Access system commands.
say [Computer] Repair computer core.
say [Computer] Return to root menu.
say Log out.
use comp_port        # under the carrier (br_term)
talk
say Reactivate the droid.
say Optimize droid's weaponry.
say Optimize droid's targeting systems.
say Activate droid's shields.
say =Leave it alone.
use TDROID3          # on the other path up
talk
say Reactivate the droid.
say Optimize droid's weaponry.
say =Leave it alone.
use TDROID           # the open ground
talk
use g_tressklcorp005 # its skeletal corpse
say Reactivate the droid.
say =Leave it alone.
use TDROID2          # the last before the Zhugs' wreck
talk
say =Who are you?    # Dezanti Zhug (tr_zhugtalk): on the way Atton's two
say You really think you can take on Mira? # reports and Mira's mines
say There's no way I'm going to surrender to you.
to tr_zhugtalk
talk
fight 30             # Dezanti and his two brothers (duros_bh)
use zhug_chest       # the Zhugs' camp
use MilHighPlstcCylin
use millowwreckage   # the wreckage up the path left, the corpse behind it
use g_tressklcorp006
exit To_402          # into the jungle
module 402dxn
save dxun_jungle
